#DESCRIPTION
Full PIC (kinetic ions AND kinetic electrons) parallel whistler-Alfven wave
test. The standard Maxwell/GMRES field solver advances E and B; both ion and
electron species are kinetic, so this exercises the full electromagnetic PIC
dispersion (electron + ion contributions) on the same whistler eigenmode used
by the hybrid version (PARAM.in.hybrid).

Same geometry/normalization as the hybrid variant. In CODE (normalized) units
d_i ~ 1, v_A ~ 1, B = Omega_i ~ 1; box Lx = 6.4 d_i, dt*Omega_i = 0.02 << 1.
Physical inputs (n = 5 amu/cc, B = 5.22 nT, v_A ~ 51 km/s, d_i ~ 102 km) are
solar-wind-like. The two kinetic species are ions (q = m = 1) and electrons
(q = -1, m = 1/1836) so the full whistler dispersion is reproduced.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Full electromagnetic PIC: standard Maxwell/GMRES field solver advances E and B;
no hybrid Ohm's-law advance.
#SOLVEEM
T                       solveEM

Two kinetic species: ions (q = 1, m = 1) and electrons (q = -1, m = 1/1836).
The electron is kinetic here (unlike the hybrid variant where it is a fluid),
so the PIC Maxwell solve carries the full whistler dispersion.
#PLASMA
2                       nS
1.0                     mass           Species 0: ions
1.0                     charge
1.0/1836.0              mass           Species 1: electrons
-1.0                    charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]          ~ ions, code T ~ 0.2 (T_code = k_B T/uNorm^2)
2.5552e-5               rho [amu/cc]   Species 1: electrons (n_e = n_i = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
5.4574                  T [K]          ~ electrons, code T ~ 0.2 (same T_code as ions)
5.2195e-9               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

Same transverse circularly-polarized whistler seed (frac = 0.02) and Alfven
velocity kick as the hybrid variant, applied to both species.
#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] ~ v_A so v_A ~ 1 in code units

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
1000                    nParticle per cell in X   (ions)
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z
1000                    nParticle per cell in X   (electrons)
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
100                     dn
-1                      dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
13.0                    TimeMax     ~1 whistler period (T ~ 13 s for the n=1 mode)

#RUN
